A||||18||voyagerspe||I have finished my motor swap ||||7||
Z||000000||voyagerspe||03-07-2001||10:15 PM||||Hi<BR>this is my first post, Ive been lurking for quite awhile and I want to thank everyone for the volumes of information that everyone has shared.  I have FINISHED (sort of) my 87 gt today.  This is what I did I bought the ARI 3.4 short block which they make from a 2.8 <BR>I installed, mustang injectors, sprint manifolds, ocelot exhaust, the big bore throttle body(from the fiero store),the heads were ported and polished. accel wires, modual,  and coil, and roller rocker arms.  I also installed the Grandam front brake upgrade with a blazer master cylender and new fiero rear brakes. I installed new shocks in the front. And ill have the rear struts and a set of comp T/A installed when the snow melts.  oh and most important I installed an 85 intake so I could put a "fiero 3.4" decal on the engine(That decal ads lot of horsepower). <BR>Im going to try to post some pics I hope this works      ||||reg||7
Z||000001||MontanaFiero||03-07-2001||10:26 PM||||Congrats on the engine swap. May you get many speeding tickets  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> lol. And welcome to the forum. This ARI 3.4L. tell me more. I assume from what you are saying you didn't have to re-locate the starter? Where can I find out more info on this?<BR>BTW- for pictures, scroll to the bottom of this page and click on the little blue box that says"Pennock's Image Poster". It's free, and if you use Windows, it will help you post your picts.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/blee291/platemt.jpg">  <BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||14
