Z||000017||Raydar||03-09-2001||10:34 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by StuGood:<BR><B>...Also - puts me to shame - takes me forever to get even little jobs done...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Don't I know THAT feeling...<P>Voyagerspe,<BR>Welcome to the Forum!<BR>Nice looking conversion. Nice work and nice car. <BR>Does your engine use a standard 3.4 crank and an overbored block?<BR>When we first heard of a 2.8 block being bored that far, many folks were a little ummm... apprehensive. <BR>How thin did that overbore leave your cylinder walls? <BR>What kind of warranty does ARI offer?<BR>Always looking for ideas. <BR>Thanks!<P>  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 03-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||stsmithgt||03-09-2001||11:53 AM||||Oh that's nice.  I like those headers.  I seem to have a strange attraction for that car too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpic_2.jpg">  Good luck with that 2.8 upgrade, which explains why the starter isn't moved. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 03-09-2001).]||||reg||1
